 58510, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MNdZq3ib6UKgwYqPHEFbGf", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62662, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments back to its last healthy release and opened the SEV2. The service is healthy again, with the error rate down from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called \"payments,\" so I checked likely names. The affected one is `payments-api`. This morning's v5.1.0 release was running in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and showed as unhealthy.\n- **Rollback:** I rolled `payments-api` back to v5.0.0 in all regions. It's the only release before v5.1.0 and the most recent one that was healthy in production. Because it's a previously healthy version, change-manager approval wasn't needed.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to create the incident timed out. No incident appeared afterward, so I retried with the same idempotency key, which prevents a duplicate. That created **INC-0001** (SEV2, `payments-api`), and on-call has been paged. The incident notes that the next step is finding the root cause of the v5.1.0 problem.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018cC5jRpnjPsgH2M89f1Xzh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01DddCyafytWYJJKygFij8Ew", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Dhaco7nKwsdx9T3ZZs1aA7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01PL4Hc